This product also includes anatomical 3D meshes and nomenclature that are NOT
covered by the Apache License. They come from two unrelated open datasets, and
they are under two different Creative Commons licences.

The male atlas — `manifest.json`, `*_male.glb` —
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International:

  BodyParts3D — The Database Center for Life Science (DBCLS), Japan
                CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan
  Z-Anatomy   — the libre 3D atlas of anatomy, derived from BodyParts3D
                CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://www.z-anatomy.com/

Anatria3D's adaptations of those meshes are themselves CC BY-SA 4.0.
Redistributing them requires preserving this attribution and keeping them under
that licence.

The female atlas — `manifest_female.json`, `*_female.glb` —
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International:

  Human Reference Atlas 3D Reference Organ Library
              HuBMAP Consortium / NIH — https://humanatlas.io/
              ref-organ/united-female v1.5, CC BY 4.0
  Visible Human Female
              U.S. National Library of Medicine, the underlying dataset
              (Spitzer & Whitlock, 2002)

Anatria3D's adaptations of those meshes remain CC BY 4.0. Redistributing them
requires preserving this attribution; there is no share-alike obligation.

The two must not be combined into one file — doing so would impose share-alike
on material whose authors chose attribution alone. The full attribution ships
with the data, in `anatomy/NOTICE` and `anatomy/LICENSE`, and is summarised for
readers in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

